    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Feed Health Monitor for WooCommerce allows you to scan your catalog for potential issues that would prevent your products from being listed successfully on Google Shopping, Facebook, or other marketing feeds.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/feed-health-monitor</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress</li>\n<li>Navigate to WooCommerce &gt; Feed Health</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"does%20this%20plugin%20generate%20a%20feed%3F\">\nDoes this plugin generate a feed?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No, this plugin only monitors your catalog for data issues.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Helps WooCommerce store owners find product data issues that may negatively affect product feeds.",
    "description": "<p>Feed Health Monitor for WooCommerce allows you to scan your catalog for potential issues that would prevent your products from being listed successfully on Google Shopping, Facebook, or other marketing feeds.</p>\n",
